	(text "C1 at U1 VDD (58), C2 at U1 AVDD (37), C3 at U2 pin 14"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 325.12 236.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "287082c5-07fa-5928-86f3-1bc0a942d526")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups: R1-R8 PA0-7, R9-R16 PB0-7, R17-R21 PC1-5, R22 MODE1/PC6, R23 MODE0/PC7. R24 keeps the chip in reset until the Pico runs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 269.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ee8b1ad8-dcb2-5cf5-845d-6147abf38877")
	)
	(text "HOW IT WORKS: both MODE pins pulled up -> chip boots from 64 KB external ROM (served by the Pico on AD0-7/A8-14).\nThe reader code jumps to its 8000h mirror and drives PC7 low; PC7 is tied to MODE0, so the internal\n16 KB mask ROM appears at 0000h and is sent as Intel HEX on PC0/TxD at f_clk/96 baud (65104 @ 6.25 MHz).\nX1/X2 and /RESET need >= 4 V, hence the 74HCT04 at 5 V. Chip pin numbers are QFP-64 (GF-3BE) pins;\nU1's footprint is the 900-mil DIP-64 of a QFP64->DIP64 adapter, pin N = QFP pin N. Pico 2 GPIOs are 5 V tolerant."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ef97b5c0-6f24-5a13-af3c-9c5844a8ca96")
	)
